                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Duloxetine (Cymbalta) and Venlafaxine (Effexor) are SNRIs in the SNRIs you were asked to learn because they are in the top 200 most prescribed medications in Australia.&nbsp;\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Like other SNRIs Duloxetine (Cymbalta) and Venlafaxine (Effexor) block the reuptake of noradrenalin and serotonin (5HT)</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "SNRIs produce less sedation and fewer cardiovascular and antimuscarinic side effects as compared to TCAs\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NO, THE CLIENT MUST BE WITHDRAWN SLOWLY!</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Your answer was correct. Always withdraw SNRIs and other antidepressants slowly.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>SNRIs have the advantage over other antidepressants that you can simply stop taking the medication after the depression has resolved.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                }
              ],
