                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Lithium has a very narrow therapeutic range\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Lithium is nephrotoxic, so as with all nephrotoxic medications, even if it is not indicated on the label, NSAIDs and other nephrotoxic agents must be avoided and the client must drink plenty of water\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Plasma concentrations of lithium must be monitored closely to avoid toxicity, which includes cardiac dysrhythmias, convulsions and renal failure\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, lithium carbonate (lithium) is better for the mania than the depression.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Your answer was correct; lithium carbonate (Lithium) is better for the mania than the depression.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Lithium is better for the depressive portion of the client's disorder than the mania</div>\n"
                }
              ],
